"text": "Your problems feel huge. The email, the bill, what they said about you, now zoom out, out of the room, over the city, past the clouds, until the whole earth is a blue dot spinning in the dark. Marcus Aurelius, Emperor of Rome, did this on purpose. In his private notes, he kept reminding himself how small and brief everything is, compared to all of time and space, not to feel worthless, to feel free. So tonight when it gets heavy, zoom out, save this for a heavy day.",
